edge identity changing with the rotating member, not of an old contact set giving way to a new one - the removed and added samples list the same external nodes re-attached to a different member. At the prescribed 5000 half-window, group-level turnover is a smooth U-shape peaking at only 0.434 with ~30/40 contacts shared across the candidate point: gradual background rotation, not an abrupt transition. Confounder controls: the bandwidth-2000 peak_change of 1.0 at t=53607 is spurious, comparing just 2 contacts against 30 during the 54607-57606 activity trough; and the external hubs show near-identical degree in the first vs last 5000-unit windows, ruling out a popularity shift in the partners.", "confidence": 0.87, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "The evidence resolves clearly. Key finding: the group's *external contact pool is essentially constant*, while group *membership* rotates through time.\n\n- **Members are time-disjoint bursts**: node 431 fires 90 of its 92 events in [39607, 44607] then goes silent (step_12); node 1783 is silent until [64608, 69607] where it fires 90 events (step_13). Each member has ~92\u201397 events / ~32\u201337 partners over the period (step_06).\n- **But they all talk to the same people**: 431's 32 neighbours and 1783's 32 neighbours share ~